HB0175

Wyoming veterans museum capital 25LSO-0190, 1.0
construction.
Description of appropriation:
The appropriation to the Legislative Service Office will be expended for the
payment of salary, per diem and mileage for the four legislators appointed to the
task force. The above estimate assumes meeting days in FY 2025 through FY 2028.
It is assumed that $5,400 ($2,300 from the 0100 series and $3,100 from the 0200
series) will be expended in FY 2028, resulting in total expenditures over the 4
years of $24,300.
DETAIL OF APPROPRIATION
Agency #: 001 Agency Name: Governor's Office
Unit: Gov.'s Office Task Forces
EXPENDITURE BY SERIES AND YEAR FY 2025 FY 2026 FY 2027
0200 Supportive Services Costs $1,389 $8,333 $8,333
Total Expenditure Per Year: $1,389 $8,333 $8,333
Grand Total Expenditure: $18,055
Total Appropriated to Agency: $25,000
Total Appropriated by Fund:
GENERAL FUND $25,000
Description of appropriation:
The appropriation to the Governor’s Office will be expended for the payment of
per diem and travel expenses for the non-legislative members of the task force.
The above estimate assumes meeting days in FY 2025 through FY 2028. It is assumed
that $6,945 will be expended in FY 2028, resulting in total expenditures over the
4 years of $25,000.
NOTICE-AGENCY ESTIMATE OF ADMINISTRATIVE IMPACT REQUESTED
This bill has administrative impact that appears to increase duties or
responsibilities of one or more state agencies and may impact agency spending or
staffing requirements. As introduced, the bill does not modify any state agency
budget or current personnel authorizations.
The following state agencies will be asked to provide their estimate of the
administrative fiscal impact prior to the first committee meeting held to
consider the bill:
State Construction Department
